---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
import dati from '../../data/gregge-tappe.json';

// Reinforcement learning: lo stesso gregge di Learn, visto dall'alto. A sinistra il ciclo dell'agente, le tappe del training e la gara. La simulazione è src/lib/gregge.ts
const COME: [string, string][] = [
  ['What is this?', 'A real reinforcement learning agent, running in your browser. Nobody shows the dog what good herding looks like. It tries moves, gets points, and its weights slowly change to earn more points. On the neural network page, the network receives the right answer for each point. Here there is no right answer, only a score that arrives later.'],
  ['What is a policy?', 'The rule that turns what the dog reads into a move. Here it is a small network. About 4 times a second it reads some numbers and picks a move: one of 9 for policy 1, one of 17 for policy 2, which can also walk slowly. A policy is the result of training, and it has only what training gave it: the reward shapes what it wants, and its inputs limit what it can notice.'],
  ['How does it learn?', 'The dog plays many games at once. After each batch, the moves that went better than expected become more likely, and the others less likely. This method is called PPO. Both policies took 4 million decisions, a few hours on a CPU, once, before this page was published. Your browser only plays the result.'],
  ['What is the reward?', 'Points when the flock gets closer to the circle and when a sheep enters. Points lost when a sheep leaves, and a little as time passes. A prize when all 180 are inside.\nA prize at the end alone would not work: a dog that moves at random almost never gets all 180 inside, so it would have nothing to learn from.\nIn policy 2 the last sheep are worth more: the last one is worth about 5 times the average, and losing it costs the same.'],
  ['How did policy 1 fail?', 'On average it looked good: it finished 88 of 100 new fields. The average hid precise errors. On some fields it got most of the flock inside and then lost it. On others it stood still, or ran for 3 minutes without closing. It reads only 18 numbers, such as the centre of the flock and the farthest sheep. When the flock splits, those numbers say little about where the pieces are.'],
  ['What changed in training?', 'Policy 2 was trained with a second reading of the field: two maps of 256 cells around the dog, one for the sheep outside the circle and one for those inside. It got 8 slow moves. The last sheep are worth more, about 5 times the average for the very last one. Games can continue with a new circle, and half of them start near the end, where policy 1 made its errors.\nMore punishment did not help: with points lost for each exit and each second, the dog almost stopped touching the sheep, so I stopped that run.'],
  ['What did it gain?', 'On 300 new fields, policy 2 finished 299 and policy 1 finished 266, with a median of 25 seconds against 46.\nWith a stone thrown at the flock after 10 seconds, which training never saw, it finished all 60 fields against 28. When the circle moves and the flock stays where it is, it finished 230 of 235 games against 98 of 171. It is still not perfect, and it is not proof that it beats people: try it.'],
  ['Does it depend on this view?', 'No. It uses no images and no camera. It reads only numbers about the flock, the dog, the circle and the obstacles, so the view is only for you. In the valley on the Learn page, the same weights can guide the dog while you turn the scene.'],
];
---
<Base title="Reinforcement learning · Riccardo Mondi" description="Two policies herd 180 sheep. See where the first fails and what fixes it." tono="neutro" largo>
  <main class="rn">
    <section class="schermo" data-gregge data-dati={JSON.stringify(dati)}>
      <header class="testa">
        <h1>Teach a dog to herd with rewards</h1>
        <a href="#how-it-works" class="mono">how it works ↓</a>
        <p class="mono messaggio">A policy turns what the dog reads into a move. Two policies, same task: see where the first fails, and what fixes it.</p>
        <p class="mono messaggio solo-tel">You can watch and play here, but it works better on a computer.</p>
      </header>

      <div class="banco">
        <canvas class="tela-gregge" role="img" aria-label="Two meadows seen from above with the same field: 180 sheep, an orange dog and a dashed circle. Sheep inside the circle turn blue. Orange marks show what each policy reads. Below, a chart of the sheep inside over time."></canvas>
        <p class="mono nota-tel" aria-live="polite"></p>

        <div class="pannello">
          <div class="mono sezione">
            <span class="titolino">the policy</span>
            <ol class="racconto">
              <li data-spiega="Policy 1 reads 18 numbers: where the dog, the flock, the circle and the nearest obstacles are. Policy 2 reads the same numbers plus two maps of 256 cells around the dog: the sheep outside the circle and the sheep inside. No images, no camera.">it reads what it can see</li>
              <li data-spiega="Stand still, or go in one of 8 directions, about 4 times a second. Policy 2 can also walk slowly in each direction, so it has 17 moves.">it picks a move</li>
              <li data-spiega="Points when the flock gets closer to the circle and when a sheep enters. Points lost when one leaves, and a little as time passes. A prize when all 180 are inside.">training rewards what worked</li>
            </ol>
            <div class="vivo">
              <canvas class="bussola" role="img" aria-label="How much policy 2 wants each move right now" data-spiega="What policy 2 wants right now. A longer arrow means a more likely move, and the square in the middle is standing still."></canvas>
              <div>
                <button type="button" class="vede" data-spiega="Orange marks what each policy reads. Dashed lines: the centre of the flock and the farthest sheep. Orange and blue cells: the maps of the sheep outside and inside, which only policy 2 has. It is why policy 1 can miss a split flock.">what the dog sees</button>
                <p class="lettura stato"></p>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>

          <div class="mono sezione">
            <span class="titolino">where policy 1 fails</span>
            <div class="tappe">
              <button type="button" data-campo="nuovo" data-spiega="A new random field, on both meadows.">new field</button>
              {dati.campi.map(c => <button type="button" data-campo={c.id}>{c.nome}</button>)}
            </div>
            <p class="spiega nota-campo"></p>
            <div class="riga comandi">
              <button type="button" class="pausa">pause</button>
              <button type="button" class="un-passo" data-spiega="Moves both dogs by one decision.">one step</button>
              <div class="passi" role="group" aria-label="Speed"><button type="button" data-vel="1">1x</button><button type="button" data-vel="4">4x</button></div>
            </div>
            <div class="tappe piccole" role="group" aria-label="Training stage of both policies" data-spiega="Replays both policies at this point of their training, on the same field.">
              <span>both policies at</span>
              {dati.tappe.map(t => <button type="button" data-tappa={t.id}>{t.nome}</button>)}
            </div>
          </div>

          <div class="mono sezione">
            <span class="titolino">beat the AI</span>
            <button type="button" class="gioca" data-spiega="A new field. You play the left meadow, policy 2 plays the right one, at the same time."></button>
            <p class="lettura esito" aria-live="polite"></p>
            <p class="lettura">your best <span class="best-uomo"></span> · AI best <span class="best-ai"></span></p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="mono tag-punto" hidden></div>
    </section>

    <section class="spiegone" id="how-it-works">
      <h2 class="mono">how it works</h2>
      {COME.map(([domanda, testo]) => <article><h3>{domanda}</h3>{testo.split('\n').map(p => <p>{p}</p>)}</article>)}
    </section>
  </main>
</Base>

<script>
  import { monta } from '../../scripts/greggeVista';
  const radice = document.querySelector<HTMLElement>('[data-gregge]')!, d = JSON.parse(radice.dataset.dati!);
  monta(radice, d.tappe, d.campi, d.migliorAI);
</script>

<style>
  :global(html) { scroll-behavior: smooth; }
  .rn { padding: 4px 24px 0; }
  .schermo { display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: var(--s2); height: calc(100vh - 62px); min-height: 560px; padding-bottom: var(--s2); }
  .testa { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; align-items: baseline; justify-content: space-between; gap: 4px var(--s2); }
  .testa a { color: var(--fg); font-size: 12px; white-space: nowrap; }
  .messaggio { flex: 1 1 100%; margin: 0; color: var(--muted); font-size: 13px; line-height: 1.45; }
  h1 { margin: 0; font-size: 24px; font-weight: 400; line-height: 1.15; }
  button { padding: 5px 12px; border: 1px solid var(--line); background: var(--bg); color: var(--muted); font: inherit; cursor: pointer; transition: color .12s, border-color .12s; }
  button:hover:not(:disabled) { border-color: var(--fg); color: var(--fg); }
  button[hidden] { display: none; }
  button[aria-pressed="true"] { border-color: var(--fg); color: var(--fg); }
  .titolino { display: block; margin-bottom: 6px; color: var(--fg); font-size: 14px; }
  .titolino::before { content: '// '; color: var(--muted); }
  .spiega { margin: 0; min-height: 4.2em; color: var(--muted); font-size: 12px; line-height: 1.45; }
  .banco { position: relative; flex: 1 1 0; min-height: 0; }
  .tela-gregge { position: absolute; inset: 0; width: 100%; height: 100%; touch-action: pan-y; }
  .pannello { position: absolute; left: 0; top: 0; bottom: 0; z-index: 1; display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: var(--s2); width: clamp(320px, 30%, 400px); overflow: hidden auto; }
  .sezione + .sezione { padding-top: var(--s2); border-top: 1px solid var(--line); }
  .sezione { font-size: 13px; color: var(--fg); }
  .riga { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; align-items: center; gap: 8px 12px; }
  .gioca { min-width: 112px; padding: 7px 16px; background: var(--fg); border-color: var(--fg); color: var(--bg); font-size: 15px; }
  .gioca:hover:not(:disabled) { background: var(--bg); border-color: var(--fg); color: var(--fg); }
  .racconto { margin: 0 0 8px; padding-left: 20px; color: var(--muted); font-size: 12px; line-height: 1.6; }
  .vivo { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 62px minmax(0, 1fr); gap: 12px; align-items: center; }
  .bussola { display: block; width: 62px; height: 62px; }
  .passi { display: inline-flex; align-items: center; gap: 4px; margin-top: 4px; }
  .passi span { margin-right: 4px; color: var(--muted); font-size: 12px; }
  .passi button { min-width: 34px; padding: 3px 6px; }
  .lettura { min-height: 1.4em; margin: 2px 0 0; color: var(--fg); font-size: 12px; }
  .tappe { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 4px; margin-bottom: 8px; }
  .tappe button { padding: 4px 8px; font-size: 12px; }
  .piccole { align-items: center; margin: 8px 0 0; }
  .piccole span { color: var(--muted); font-size: 12px; }
  .comandi { margin-top: 6px; font-size: 12px; }
  .comandi button { padding: 4px 8px; }
  .vede { padding: 4px 8px; font-size: 12px; }
  .nota-tel, .solo-tel { display: none; }
  .tag-punto { position: fixed; left: 0; top: 0; z-index: 5; max-width: 300px; padding: 4px 8px; background: var(--bg); border: 1px solid var(--fg); color: var(--fg); font-size: 12px; line-height: 1.45; pointer-events: none; }
  .tag-punto[hidden] { display: none; }
  .spiegone { max-width: 720px; margin: 0 auto; padding: var(--s4) 0; border-top: 1px solid var(--line); scroll-margin-top: var(--s2); }
  .spiegone h2 { margin: 0 0 var(--s3); font-size: 14px; font-weight: 400; color: var(--fg); }
  .spiegone h2::before { content: '// '; color: var(--muted); }
  .spiegone article { margin-bottom: var(--s3); }
  .spiegone h3 { margin: 0 0 4px; font-size: 16px; font-weight: 400; color: var(--fg); }
  .spiegone p { margin: 0 0 var(--s1); color: var(--muted); font-size: 14px; line-height: 1.7; }
  @media (max-width: 760px) {
    .rn { padding: 0 16px; }
    .schermo { height: auto; min-height: 0; gap: var(--s1); padding-bottom: var(--s3); }
    h1 { font-size: 20px; }
    .banco { display: contents; }
    .testa { order: 0; }
    .tela-gregge { position: static; display: block; order: 1; width: 100%; height: calc(184vw + 90px); max-height: 900px; }
    .pannello { position: static; order: 3; width: 100%; overflow: visible; }
    .gioca { flex: 1 1 100%; width: 100%; padding: 10px; }
    .tag-punto { display: none !important; }
    .solo-tel { display: block; }
    .nota-tel { display: block; order: 2; min-height: 1.5em; margin: 0; color: var(--arancio); font-size: 12px; line-height: 1.45; }
  }
</style>
